{"parentUuid":"eefc7705-a2f1-42db-9012-8e63d5e8a2d6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"27b49a96-c58d-4815-8ac6-e1321b974a0c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9rYBHMMWvRKEYcbDpEZja","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"body\":\"`LoadAgentTypeHint`'s docstring says it returns empty when the value \\\"isn't a registered agent type\\\", but the implementation currently returns the trimmed file contents without validating it against known/registered agent types. Either validate (e.g., via `agent.GetByAgentType` / a known-type check) or update the comment so callers don't rely on stronger semantics than are actually implemented.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:39Z\",\"line\":355,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/session_state.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"Lock files are only removed by `strategy.ClearSessionState`, but stale-session cleanup happens via `session.StateStore.Load` calling `store.Clear(...)`, which won’t touch `entire-locks/`. That means `entire-locks/\\u003csession\\u003e.lock` files can accumulate over time even as stale sessions are deleted. Consider adding a best-effort lock-file cleanup path in the stale-session deletion flow (e.g., in `session.StateStore.Clear` or a shared helper) so lock artifacts don’t grow unbounded.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:39Z\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/session_state.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"These hard-coded Unix-style paths will make this test OS-dependent. On Windows, `filepath.Separator` is `\\\\`, and `filepath.Abs` will normalize differently, so `pathHasDirPrefix` likely won't match and the test will fail. Consider building `sessionDir`/`transcript` using `filepath.FromSlash` (or `filepath.Join` with OS separators) so the prefix logic is exercised portably across platforms.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-30T10:04:40Z\",\"line\":173,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/registry_test.go\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"### Banner suppressed when first claimer lacks HookResponseWriter\\n\\n**Medium Severity**\\n\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION START --\\u003e\\nIn the Cursor-forwarding scenario, `claimedFirst` gates both session ownership and banner display. `CursorAgent` does not implement `HookResponseWriter`. When Cursor wins the `StoreAgentTypeHint` race (~50% of the time), it gets `claimedFirst=true` but can't write a banner. Claude Code then gets `claimedFirst=false` and its banner is suppressed. The user never sees the \\\"Entire CLI will link this conversation\\\" message. Before this change, Claude Code's process always showed the banner. The test uses `mockHookResponseAgent` for both agents, masking this production mismatch.\\n\\u003c!-- DESCRIPTION END --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: edd0dd7a-d003-48b3-9bd2-6ee9db8c54ef --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- LOCATIONS START\\ncmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go#L150-L159\\ncmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go#L114-L122\\nLOCATIONS END --\\u003e\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eAdditional Locations (1)\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\n- [`cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go#L114-L122`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/9f34898bf984f8a4c6d2e6c0ac789e68920357b2/cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go#L114-L122)\\n\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003cdiv\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Fix in Cursor\\\" width=\\\"115\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" src=\\\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href=\\\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\u003e\\u003cpic