{"parentUuid":"6e65efed-dc79-422b-99b8-2254e0eaf0a2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"1\t# Entire - CLI\n2\t\n3\tThis repo contains the CLI for Entire.\n4\t\n5\t## Architecture\n6\t\n7\t- CLI built with github.com/spf13/cobra and github.com/charmbracelet/huh\n8\t\n9\t## Key Directories\n10\t\n11\t### Commands (`cmd/`)\n12\t\n13\t- `entire/`: Main CLI entry point\n14\t- `entire/cli`: CLI utilities and helpers (Cobra commands, helpers, group roots)\n15\t- `entire/cli/commands`: actual command implementations\n16\t- `entire/cli/agent`: agent implementations (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI) - see [Agent Integration Checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) and [Agent Implementation Guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md)\n17\t- `entire/cli/strategy`: strategy implementation (manual-commit) - see section below\n18\t- `entire/cli/checkpoint`: checkpoint storage abstractions (temporary and committed)\n19\t- `entire/cli/session`: session state management\n20\t- `entire/cli/integration_test`: integration tests (simulated hooks)\n21\t- `e2e/`: E2E tests with real agent calls (see [e2e/README.md](e2e/README.md))\n22\t\n23\t### Command Layout\n24\t\n25\tThe CLI is organized around five noun groups plus a small set of top-level\n26\tverbs. The groups are the canonical home for each verb; legacy top-level\n27\tshortcuts remain functional but hidden, and emit a deprecation hint pointing\n28\tat the canonical group form.\n29\t\n30\t- `session` (alias: `sessions`): `list`, `info`, `stop`, `attach`, `resume`, `current`\n31\t- `checkpoint` (aliases: `cp`, `checkpoints`): `list`, `explain`, `rewind`, `search`\n32\t- `agent`: bare opens the interactive agent selector, plus `list`, `add`, `remove`\n33\t- `configure`: bare prints help and a hint pointing at `entire agent`; flags\n34\t  manage non-agent settings (telemetry, git-hook installation mode, strategy\n35\t  options, summary provider). Agent CRUD lives under `entire agent`.\n36\t- `auth`: `login`, `logout`, `status`, `list`, `revoke`\n37\t- `doctor`: bare runs the scan-and-fix flow, plus `trace`, `logs`, `bundle`\n38\t\n39\tTop-level lifecycle and standalone commands: `enable`, `disable`, `status`,\n40\t`login`, `logout`, `clean`, `version`, `dispatch`, `activity`, `help`,\n41\t`configure`.\n42\t\n43\tHidden top-level shortcuts (functional, emit a one-line deprecation hint):\n44\t`rewind` → `checkpoint rewind`, `resume` → `session resume`, `attach` →\n45\t`session attach`, `explain` → `checkpoint explain`, `trace` → `doctor trace`.\n46\tCobra-native aliases (no hint): `sessions` → `session`, `cp`/`checkpoints` →\n47\t`checkpoint`. The `search` top-level remains hidden without a hint.\n48\t\n49\tDeprecated top-level alias (functional, prints cobra deprecation message):\n50\t`reset` → `clean`.\n51\t\n52\tHidden infrastructure commands: `hooks`, `migrate`, `trail`,\n53\t`curl-bash-post-install`, `__send_analytics`.\n54\t\n55\tThe `hideAsAlias(cmd, canonical)` helper in `cmd/entire/cli/aliascmd.go`\n56\tmarks a command Hidden and sets cobra's `Deprecated` field so the hint\n57\trenders to stderr on every invocation while the command stays functional.\n58\tDiagnostic subcommands live alongside `doctor.go` as `doctor_logs.go` and\n59\t`doctor_bundle.go`. Group roots and noun-group children live in files\n60\tnamed `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go` respectively.\n61\t\n62\t## Tech Stack\n63\t\n64\t- Language: Go 1.26.x\n65\t- Build tool: mise, go modules\n66\t- Linting: golangci-lint\n67\t\n68\t## Development\n69\t\n70\t### Running Tests\n71\t\n72\t```bash\n73\tmise run test\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\t### Running Integration Tests\n77\t\n78\t```bash\n79\tmise run test:integration\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t### Running All Tests (CI)\n83\t\n84\t```bash\n85\tmise run test:ci\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tThis runs unit tests, integration tests, and the E2E canary (Vogon agent) in sequence. Integration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n89\t\n90\t### Running E2E Canary Tests (Vogon Agent)\n91\t\n92\tThe Vogon agent is a deterministic fake agent that exercises the full E2E test suite without making any API calls. Named after the Vogons from The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy — bureaucratic, procedural, and deterministic to a fault.\n93\t\n94\t```bash\n95\tmise run test:e2e:canary           # Run all E2E tests with the Vogon agent\n96\tmise run test:e2e:canary TestFoo   # Run a specific test\n97\t```\n98\t\n99\t- **Runs as part of `test:ci`** — canary failures block merges\n100\t- **No API calls, no cost** — safe to run freely, unlike real agent E2E tests\n101\t- **If a canary test fails, the bug is in the CLI or test infrastructure**, not in an agent\n102\t- Located in `e2e/vogon/` (binary) and `cmd/entire/cli/agent/vogon/` (Agent interface)\n103\t- The binary parses prompts via regex, creates/modifies/deletes files, and fires lifecycle hooks\n104\t- **IMPORTANT: When changing E2E test prompt wording**, the Vogon binary (`e2e/vogon/main.go`) parses prompts with hardcoded regexes. New phrasing may not match existing patterns — always run `mise run test:e2e:canary` after changing prompt text and fix Vogon's parsing if tests fail.\n105\t\n106\t### Running E2E Tests (Only When Explicitly Requested)\n107\t\n108\t**IMPORTANT: Do NOT run E2E tests proactively.** E2E tests make real API calls to agents, which consume tokens and cost money. Only run them when the user explicitly asks for E2E testing.\n109\t\n110\t```bash\n111\tmise run test:e2e [filter]                          # All agents, filtered\n112\tmise run test:e2e --agent claude-code [filter]       # Claude Code only\n113\tmise run test:e2e --agent gemini-cli [filter]        # Gemini CLI only\n114\tmise run test:e2e --agent opencode [filter]          # OpenCode only\n115\tmise run test:e2e --agent cursor [filter]            # Cursor only\n116\tmise run test:e2e --agent factoryai-droid [filter]   # Factory AI Droid only\n117\tmise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli [filter]       # Copilot CLI only\n118\t```\n119\t\n120\tE2E tests:\n121\t\n122\t- Use the `//go:build e2e` build tag\n123\t- Located in `e2e/tests/`\n124\t- See [`e2e/README.md`](e2e/README.md) for full documentation (structure, debugging, adding agents)\n125\t- Test real agent interactions (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, or Vogon creating files, committing, etc.)\n126\t- Validate checkpoint scenarios documented in `docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md`\n127\t- Support multiple agents via `E2E_AGENT` env var (`claude-code`, `gemini`, `opencode`, `cursor`, `factoryai-droid`, `copilot-cli`, `vogon`)\n128\t\n129\t**Environment variables:**\n130\t\n131\t- `E2E_AGENT` - Agent to test with (default: `claude-code`)\n132\t- `E2E_CLAUDE_MODEL` - Claude model to use (default: `haiku` for cost efficiency)\n133\t- `E2E_TIMEOUT` - Timeout per prompt (default: `2m`)\n134\t\n135\t### Test Parallelization\n136\t\n137\t**Always use `t.Parallel()` in tests.** Every top-level test function and subtest should call `t.Parallel()` unless it modifies process-global state (e.g., `os.Chdir()`).\n138\t\n139\t```go\n140\tfunc TestFeature_Foo(t *testing.T) {\n141\t    t.Parallel()\n142\t    // ...\n143\t}\n144\t\n145\t// Integration tests with TestEnv\n146\tfunc TestFeature_Bar(t *testing.T) {\n147\t    t.Parallel()\n148\t    env := NewFeatureBranchEnv(t)\n149\t    // ...\n150\t}\n151\t```\n152\t\n153\t**Exception:** Tests that modify process-global state cannot be parallelized. This includes `os.Chdir()`/`t.Chdir()` and `os.Setenv()`/`t.Setenv()` — Go's test framework will panic if these are used after `t.Parallel()`.\n154\t\n155\t### Git in Tests\n156\t\n157\t**Tests that touch git state must use an isolated temp repo — never the real repo CWD.**\n158\t\n159\tMany handlers (lifecycle, strategy, hooks) resolve the git repo from CWD via `OpenRepository`, `GetGitCommonDir`, `DetectFileChanges`, etc. Without isolation, tests can create session state files, shadow branches, or other artifacts in the real `.git/` directory.\n160\t\n161\tUse the `testutil` helpers:\n162\t\n163\t```go\n164\ttmpDir := t.TempDir()\n165\ttestutil.InitRepo(t, tmpDir)                    // git init + user config + disable GPG\n166\ttestutil.WriteFile(t, tmpDir, \"f.txt\", \"init\")  // create a file\n167\ttestutil.GitAdd(t, tmpDir, \"f.txt\")             // stage it\n168\ttestutil.GitCommit(t, tmpDir, \"init\")           // commit (needs at least one commit for HEAD)\n\n... [572 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"30667a6c-17d8-4662-bf1b-04e74074bd92","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:54:11.230Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"318f7004-8303-4baf-a7c3-83b5e856dc5a","version":"2.1.123","gitBranch":"ashtom/cursor-fix"}
